    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "The full test suite is green (BUILD SUCCESS). \n\nI implemented the `initials` field by:\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added an `initials` property to the `Owner` schema (read-only string), so the generated `OwnerDto` gains the field.\n2. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a MapStruct `@Mapping` that computes `initials` as the upper-cased first letters of `firstName` and `lastName`, dot-separated with a trailing dot:\n\n```java\nowner.getFirstName().substring(0, 1).toUpperCase() + \".\" + owner.getLastName().substring(0, 1).toUpperCase() + \".\"\n```\n\nFor `firstName=\"john\"`, `lastName=\"smith\"` this yields `\"J.S.\"`, and the response DTO is already produced by `RespondWithOwner` via `ownerMapper.toOwnerDto(owner)`, so `GET /api/owners/{id}` now returns `$.initials`. The `coreComputesInitials` acceptance test and the rest of the suite pass.",
